      "attributes": {
        "id": 711,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both patterns use the て form to link a verb or verb phrase to the next part of the sentence, but the nuance varies. It can either simply connect actions, as in パンを買って食べた ('I bought bread and ate it'), or suggest a cause or effect, as in 人が多くて入れなかった ('There were too many people, so I couldn't get in'). This interpretation depends on the context.",
